The current bug report describes an issue in the `OpenMapRealVector.ebeMultiply(RealVector)` method where it returns wrong values when one entry of the specified `RealVector` is `NaN` or `Infinity`. The method implementation directly multiplies the entries of the vectors without handling the special cases where the entries are `NaN` or `Infinity`.

Here is the relevant code snippet of the `ebeMultiply` method:
```java
    @Override
    public OpenMapRealVector ebeMultiply(RealVector v) {
        checkVectorDimensions(v.getDimension());
        OpenMapRealVector res = new OpenMapRealVector(this);       
        for (Iterator iter = entries.iterator(); iter.hasNext();) {
            iter.advance();
            res.setEntry(iter.key(), iter.value() * v.getEntry(iter.key()));
        }
        return res;
    }
```

To fix this issue, you need to handle the special cases where the entries are `NaN` or `Infinity` in the multiplication operation.

